# Manufacturing production order.
#
# Capture the order, confirm the specification, then assign a line from the
# product. Electronics goes to the ElectronicsLine, Food to the FoodLine, and
# anything else to the GeneralLine.
# Complete inspection with "pass" to pack the batch and cancel rework. Complete
# it with "fail" to send the batch to rework and cancel packing. The order closes
# only after that branch has finished.
# Rejecting capture or the specification rejects the order: manufacturing and
# closure are cancelled. Rejecting inspection does the same, because neither
# pass nor fail was recorded.
#
# Roles are the participant role strings.

DEFINITION
PROD_ORDER|Production Order|1

WORKITEMS
process|ORDER|-|Production Order
process|PLAN|ORDER|Order Planning
task|LOG_ORDER|PLAN|Capture Order
task|CONFIRM_SPEC|PLAN|Confirm Specification
process|BUILD|ORDER|Manufacturing
task|ASSIGN_LINE|BUILD|Assign Production Line
task|PRODUCE|BUILD|Assemble Product
task|INSPECT|BUILD|Inspect Quality
task|PACK|BUILD|Pack Passed Batch
task|REWORK|BUILD|Rework Failed Batch
process|FINISH|ORDER|Order Closure
task|CLOSE_ORDER|FINISH|Close Order

DEPENDENCIES
LOG_ORDER|CONFIRM_SPEC|*
PLAN|BUILD|*
ASSIGN_LINE|PRODUCE|*
PRODUCE|INSPECT|*
INSPECT|PACK|pass
INSPECT|REWORK|fail
BUILD|FINISH|*

ROUTING
LOG_ORDER|role|Planner
CONFIRM_SPEC|role|Planner
ASSIGN_LINE|data|productLine|GeneralLine|Electronics|ElectronicsLine|Food|FoodLine
PRODUCE|role|Operator
INSPECT|role|QualityInspector
PACK|role|WarehouseHand
REWORK|role|Operator
CLOSE_ORDER|role|Planner

EXTRAS
priority|INSPECT|2
audit|INSPECT
audit|CLOSE_ORDER
deadline|INSPECT|8
